text:
- It writes receipt lines to `--receipt <path>`: ndjson, one `write_all` per line, every line `"v":1` + a kebab `kind`. The kinds are:
  - `start` {`cli_version`}: in interactive mode written after the fake agent has taken its `HostTerminal` raw-mode guard on its own stdin/stdout (as the real CLI sets raw mode itself), so tests send no key before it; print mode takes no raw-mode guard and writes it before its four fixture events
  - `size` {`cols`, `rows`}: at start and again whenever the terminal size changed (the resize oracle) — in interactive mode a watcher thread writes the size at once, then polls it every 10 ms and writes on every change, so a resize reaches the receipt with no key after it; nothing while stdin/stdout is not a terminal, and print mode writes none
  - `cwd` {`cwd`}
  - `hold` {`pid`}: the `--exit-no-eof` holder, at its start
  - `env` {`names`}: sorted, names only, never a value
  - `fds` {`fds`}: Unix only
  - `key` {`hex`}: one per byte outside a paste
  - `prompt` {`text`, `hex`, `bare_esc`, `origin` `human`|`harness`, `submit` `fired`|`suppressed`|`local-command`|`no-fixture`|`no-hooks`}
  - `hook` {`event`, `command_absolute`, `ran`, plus `exit_code`, `stderr_len`, `stdout_hex` and `stdin_hex` (the exact bytes offered on the hook's stdin) when it ran}
  - `statusline` {the `hook` kind's fields without `event`}; tests wait for it through `tests/support/fake.rs` `wait_statusline`
  - `step` {`index`, `event`}
